title: Fix gaze calibration pipeline — raw iris stream + least-squares affine
summary: 'Fixed three critical bugs in gaze calibration: (1) calibration view received already-calibrated screen-pixel stream instead of raw iris positions, training the affine on screen→screen instead of iris→screen; (2) feedback dot during calibration was off-screen due to double-scaling screen pixels as normalized coords; (3) only 3 of 5 calibration points were used. Replaced with raw iris stream, least-squares affine over all points, Kalman reset on recalibration, and enhanced debug overlay showing both raw and calibrated dots with coordinate labels.'
