  - packages/conductor/.purpose
decisions:
  - id: raw-iris-stream
    decision: Added dedicated rawIrisStream to VisionGazeProvider separate from calibrated gazePointStream
    rationale: Calibration needs ground-truth iris positions (0-1 normalized), not post-calibration screen coords. Dual streams keep the public API backward-compatible.
  - id: least-squares-affine
    decision: Replaced 3-point affine with least-squares normal equations over all collected points
    rationale: Using all 5 calibration points via least-squares is more robust and makes better use of the calibration effort the user invests.
  - id: dual-dot-debug
    decision: Debug overlay shows cyan (calibrated) + yellow (raw iris) dots with coordinate label
    rationale: User reported 'somewhat works' — needs visual feedback to diagnose remaining accuracy issues.
learnings:
  - Gaze calibration data must come from raw sensor stream, never from post-calibration output — otherwise the affine trains on its own (wrong) predictions
  - Vision framework iris positions are normalized 0-1 with Y-up; multiplying screen-pixel values by screen dimensions is a telltale sign of coordinate space confusion
  - Kalman filter must be reset after recalibration since its state/velocity estimates are in the old mapping's coordinate space
